      "title": "Aggressive fourth downs",
      "recommendation": "On 4th-and-manageable and in the gray zone for two-point conversions, default to the analytically favored aggression unless game state clearly changes the math. That means fewer automatic punts and more willingness to take the possession edge when the numbers are close.",
      "rationale": "Public win-probability and expected-points models say extra possessions are usually worth more than the reputational cost of occasional failure, and many coaches still play too conservatively.",
      "prior": {
        "belief_summaries": {
          "most_plausible_value": 0.25,
