      "title": "Two-high shells",
      "recommendation": "Use more two-high safety shells on early downs and accept some run efficiency to protect against explosives. Make offenses earn long drives rather than giving up one-play touchdowns.",
      "rationale": "Tracking-based models reward limiting explosive passes more than squeezing a few extra run stuffs, so the field-position and win-probability trade favors the lighter box more often than coaches admit.",
