      "title": "Timeout to kill chaos",
      "recommendation": "Spend a timeout before a key snap when the opponent is rushing to the line, your defense is misaligned, or a bad personnel matchup is about to get exposed. I am not leaning on clean public analytics here; this is a coaching judgment that a reset can prevent a cheap bust.",
      "rationale": "This is intuition because the payoff depends on opponent tempo, substitution discipline, and whether your sideline actually uses the timeout to get to the right call; the public evidence is thin and mixed.",
      "prior": {
        "belief_summaries": {
          "most_plausible_value": 0.0,
          "interval_95_low": -0.43,
          "interval_95_high": 0.43,
          "shape": "symmetric",
          "tails": "heavy"
        },
        "distribution_family": {
          "name": "student_t",
          "justification": "This is weakly identified and can swing either way depending on matchup and timing, so I want a symmetric heavy-tailed prior rather than a narrow one."
