      "title": "No-huddle bursts after explosives",
      "recommendation": "Use short no-huddle bursts right after chunk plays or defensive busts, then return to your base tempo. The aim is to stop substitutions, keep the defense in its worst personnel, and attack before it can fully reset.",
      "rationale": "This is intuition because public research on tempo is mixed and often confounded by matchup quality; the benefit here is in the specific sequencing, not a blanket hurry-up identity.",
      "prior": {
        "belief_summaries": {
          "most_plausible_value": 0.08,
