      "title": "Disguise-and-pressure mix",
      "recommendation": "Mix late coverage rotation with selective simulated pressure on passing downs so the quarterback does not get the same pre-snap answer every time. The goal is to create hesitation, protection errors, and throwaways without living in all-out blitz.",
      "rationale": "This is intuition because the value of disguise depends heavily on quarterback processing speed, protection rules, and opponent study, and public analytics are not definitive on the exact dose.",
      "prior": {
        "belief_summaries": {
          "most_plausible_value": 0.11,
          "interval_95_low": -0.24,
          "interval_95_high": 0.46,
          "shape": "symmetric",
          "tails": "heavy"
        },
        "distribution_family": {
